    "content": "The 2026 Social Security cost-of-living adjustment (COLA) is projected to be 2.8%. This increase, driven by consumer price index (CPI-W) data, will result in an average monthly benefit increase of about $56 for retirees. The final percentage, officially announced in October 2025, will be based on 2025 third-quarter inflation data and takes effect in January 2026. Key 2026 COLA Details: Projected Increase: 2.8%. Average Increase: Approx. $56.60 per month, raising the average check from $2,024 to $2,081. Who is Affected: Over 71 million Americans, including retirees and SSI recipients. Announcement Date: October 2025, based on Q3 inflation data. Effective Date: January 2026 for Social Security, and Dec 31, 2025, for SSI recipients. Medicare Impact: Final net increases depend on the 2026 Medicare Part B premium, which can offset part of the COLA. Note: This projection is based on early data; inflationary changes throughout 2025 could result in a final COLA higher or lower than 2.8%.",
